{"content":[{"c":["TOB"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place where Jephthah fled after his half brothers threw him out for being illegitimate (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.11.3-5","r":"Judg.11.3-5","rawR":"Judg.11.3-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.11.3-5","value":"Judg.11.3-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 11:3-5"},"). During the reign of David, the Ammonites hired 12,000 men from Tob as mercenaries to fight against David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.10.6-8","r":"2Sam.10.6-8","rawR":"2Sam.10.6-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.10.6-8","value":"2Sam.10.6-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 10:6-8"},"). It is probably the same as the Aramite kingdom named Tob, which was located in the desert east or northeast of Gilead. During the Maccabean period, a Jewish colony was located in Tob."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tob","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 11:3-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.11.3-5","rawQueryValue":"Judg.11.3-5","sourceRefExact":"Judg.11.3-5"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 10:6-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.10.6-8","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.10.6-8","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.10.6-8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"97dd2df3614e61755db5779f6d80be3db0272741c560950adcae29353bec72d6","sourceItemName":"Tob","sourceItemOrder":189,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Tob","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Tob","title":"Tob","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}